[quote="arenson9"]

 Blue Kae -- We&#39;re going to meet in person at Comic Carnival tomorrow, right? The designers of Heroes Wanted have regularly playtested it at Game Preserve Fashion Mall Commons at a monthly game designers meet up. It is quite good in my opinion. The part about joining the top and bottom is a bit of fun, but it&#39;s mostly about replayability, as you get a far wider range of heroes to play. Yes, from a theme perspective, and particuarly from a story perspective, it is much weaker. Heroes Wanted is nowhere near like the awesome story/theme of Sentinels of the Multiverse, BUT the gameplay itself is very cool -- small group tactics with constant interesting choices about using resources now versus later, taking risks or not taking risks, scoring points in different ways, all while determining the best strategy against your particular adversaries and against this particular villain. 

[/quote]

&nbsp;

We did! I had a great time today, just didn&#39;t get a chance to check the forums until now though. &nbsp;After everything I&#39;ve heard about Heroes Wanted, I&#39;ll have to take another look, possibly I was just in the wrong frame of mind when I checked it out.&nbsp;
